{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21880008",
      "title": "How Authentication Works in Vue Apps (or any SPA)",
      "lectureOrder": 263,
      "videoOrder": 234,
      "sourceHash": "614b99e2fe8cd821616b68b2c2711639fbfbfd76e4c87daf4cc6d9f2ccf88de4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 3.75,
          "en": "Before we write any code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.75,
          "end": 8.53,
          "en": "we have to understand how authentication works in Vue apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.53,
          "end": 13.38,
          "en": "or to be precise, in any single-page application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.38,
          "end": 15.12,
          "en": "Because it's a bit different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.12,
          "end": 18.99,
          "en": "than the traditional authentication you might know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.99,
          "end": 21.87,
          "en": "from websites and web applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.87,
          "end": 24.57,
          "en": "where you use some server-side language.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.57,
          "end": 25.71,
          "en": "We're not doing this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.71,
          "end": 27.26,
          "en": "Vue runs in a browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.26,
          "end": 30.02,
          "en": "therefore this will work a bit differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.02,
          "end": 34.21,
          "en": "So, we have our Vue app or any single-page application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.21,
          "end": 38.08,
          "en": "using any library or framework, doesn't have to be Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.08,
          "end": 40.21,
          "en": "and we got our backend server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.21,
          "end": 43.12,
          "en": "In our case, that's Firebase but it could be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.12,
          "end": 46.73,
          "en": "any HTTP server to which we send requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.73,
          "end": 51.04,
          "en": "Any REST API or GraphQL API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.04,
          "end": 54.29,
          "en": "Now, the thing is that on this server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.29,
          "end": 56.8,
          "en": "we have certain public resources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.8,
          "end": 59.6,
          "en": "but also some restricted resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.6,
          "end": 62.34,
          "en": "For example, in our course project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.34,
          "end": 64.9,
          "en": "we might be able to get coaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.9,
          "end": 68.95,
          "en": "and send messages to coaches without being logged in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.95,
          "end": 72.61,
          "en": "so that would be public data and public resources,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.61,
          "end": 77.42,
          "en": "which should be accessible by any visitor of this webpage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.42,
          "end": 80.45,
          "en": "no matter if you are logged in or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.45,
          "end": 83.67,
          "en": "But then, we also got some resources, some data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.67,
          "end": 86.87,
          "en": "some kinds of requests that should be restricted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.87,
          "end": 91.18,
          "en": "For example, you should only be able to register as a coach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.18,
          "end": 94.91,
          "en": "and therefore, create a new coach, if you are logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.91,
          "end": 98.71000000000001,
          "en": "The same for fetching requests, fetching messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.71000000000001,
          "end": 100.57,
          "en": "you as a coach received.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.57,
          "end": 103.233,
          "en": "Of course, you need to be logged in to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.92,
          "end": 107.25,
          "en": "So we got mixed data on our server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.25,
          "end": 110.53,
          "en": "and that's a typical scenario in most websites,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.53,
          "end": 113.83,
          "en": "you will have some data that should be accessible by anyone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.83,
          "end": 116.4,
          "en": "and some data that's restricted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.4,
          "end": 119.19,
          "en": "Now, the thing is with this setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.19,
          "end": 122.85,
          "en": "where our web application, our website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.85,
          "end": 125.11,
          "en": "is kind of detached from the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.11,
          "end": 128.82,
          "en": "it's not served by the same server and well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.82,
          "end": 131.86,
          "en": "the backend doesn't really know the front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.86,
          "end": 135.46,
          "en": "In such scenarios, the server really does not care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.46,
          "end": 138.35,
          "en": "about the clients, so about the Vue application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.35,
          "end": 140.04,
          "en": "in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.04,
          "end": 143.46,
          "en": "The server, in our case, Firebase but again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.46,
          "end": 147.02,
          "en": "you could be using any API, really does not care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.02,
          "end": 148.01,
          "en": "about our Vue app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.01,
          "end": 151.16,
          "en": "It doesn't store any information about that app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.16,
          "end": 155.67000000000002,
          "en": "It doesn't store, whether the user of this app instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.67000000000002,
          "end": 157.69299999999998,
          "en": "is actually logged in or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.76,
          "end": 163.15,
          "en": "Therefore, we'll have to find a way of still keeping track,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.15,
          "end": 165.1,
          "en": "whether the visitor of the webpage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 165.1,
          "end": 168.94,
          "en": "who's currently using the website is logged in or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.94,
          "end": 173.17000000000002,
          "en": "Now of course, it always all starts by some login data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.17000000000002,
          "end": 175.81,
          "en": "being sent from the Vue app to the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.81,
          "end": 178.18,
          "en": "We have some login page in our Vue app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.18,
          "end": 181.61,
          "en": "and once the user entered an email and a password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.61,
          "end": 184.04,
          "en": "that data is sent to the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.04,
          "end": 187.97,
          "en": "to create the user or to log the user in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.97,
          "end": 190.98,
          "en": "And now on traditional websites,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.98,
          "end": 194.68,
          "en": "the server would basically store a session,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 194.68,
          "end": 197.72,
          "en": "it would store information about that user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.72,
          "end": 201.47,
          "en": "and just send a session ID to the front end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 201.47,
          "end": 204.21,
          "en": "to the browser, so that there is a connection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.21,
          "end": 206.76,
          "en": "between the user using the site and the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.76,
          "end": 209.5,
          "en": "and the server being aware of that user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.5,
          "end": 211.82,
          "en": "However, that's not how it'll work here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.82,
          "end": 215.75,
          "en": "when you have a single-page application talking to an API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.75,
          "end": 220.1,
          "en": "Instead here, the server doesn't store any information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 220.1,
          "end": 222.07,
          "en": "and it'll do something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 222.07,
          "end": 226.14,
          "en": "It'll send back a token back to the front end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 226.14,
          "end": 228.25,
          "en": "back to the single-page application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 228.25,
          "end": 230.44,
          "en": "in our case, back to the Vue app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230.44,
          "end": 234.95,
          "en": "once that login data is validated and verified.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 234.95,
          "end": 238.17000000000002,
          "en": "So if it is a valid user who's trying to login,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 238.17000000000002,
          "end": 240.97,
          "en": "if that data could be confirmed by the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 240.97,
          "end": 243.93,
          "en": "the server generates a token which is in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 243.93,
          "end": 247.94,
          "en": "just a very long string which is sent back to the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 247.94,
          "end": 251.54,
          "en": "Now, the thing about this token is that it's created such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 251.54,
          "end": 255.76,
          "en": "that only the server is able to validate it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 255.76,
          "end": 258.56,
          "en": "Only the server will be able to tell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 258.56,
          "end": 262.26,
          "en": "if a token is valid or not because it was generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 262.26,
          "end": 266.39,
          "en": "with a certain secret key which only the server knows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.39,
          "end": 269.21,
          "en": "So this token can't be faked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.21,
          "end": 271.43,
          "en": "The token is then sent back to the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 271.43,
          "end": 273.26,
          "en": "and there, we can store it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 273.26,
          "end": 277.42,
          "en": "We can store it in Vuex or also in more permanent places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 277.42,
          "end": 279.27,
          "en": "like local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 279.27,
          "end": 283.78,
          "en": "And the thing with that token now is that it can be attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 283.78,
          "end": 287.77,
          "en": "to these outgoing requests to restrict the resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 287.77,
          "end": 289.84000000000003,
          "en": "And if that token is attached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 289.84000000000003,
          "end": 293.15,
          "en": "since only a server is able to validate the token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 293.15,
          "end": 295.76,
          "en": "if the server receives a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 295.76,
          "end": 299.12,
          "en": "to a restricted resource with a valid token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 299.12,
          "end": 301.17,
          "en": "the server will grant access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 301.17,
          "end": 304.04,
          "en": "and return the appropriate data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 304.04,
          "end": 308.33,
          "en": "If the token is invalid or missing, access is denied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 308.33,
          "end": 310.77,
          "en": "That's how authentication works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 310.77,
          "end": 314.25,
          "en": "in single-page applications talking to an API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 314.25,
          "end": 316.62,
          "en": "and that's exactly the setup we have here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 316.62,
          "end": 318.46,
          "en": "and exactly the setup you will have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 318.46,
          "end": 321.65,
          "en": "in most Vue applications you're going to build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321.65,
          "end": 323.22,
          "en": "Therefore, this is the scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 323.22,
          "end": 326.29,
          "en": "we'll have a look at in this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 326.29,
          "end": 327.66,
          "en": "Now of course in our app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 327.66,
          "end": 330.65,
          "en": "we also want to have some implications of the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 330.65,
          "end": 334.08,
          "en": "being logged in or not on our webpage itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 334.08,
          "end": 337.29,
          "en": "not just on the requests that are being sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 337.29,
          "end": 339.92,
          "en": "For example, this requests menu item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 339.92,
          "end": 343.97,
          "en": "should only be clickable if the user is logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 343.97,
          "end": 346.65999999999997,
          "en": "We should only be able to register as a coach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 346.65999999999997,
          "end": 349.49,
          "en": "with the button that is sometimes visible here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 349.49,
          "end": 351.4,
          "en": "if we are logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 351.4,
          "end": 355.2,
          "en": "Otherwise, we want to offer a login button to the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 355.2,
          "end": 358.26,
          "en": "So, these are also implications of authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 358.26,
          "end": 360.05,
          "en": "being added to the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 360.05,
          "end": 362.16,
          "en": "And with that theory out of the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 362.16,
          "end": 365.44,
          "en": "let's now step-by-step add authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 365.44,
          "end": 367.663,
          "en": "and see all of that in action.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
